One INFO line per request that leaves the scheduler finished.

vLLM 0.28.0 logs nothing when a request completes. The only request-lifecycle
lines in v1 -- "Added request", "Aborted request(s)", "Request ... aborted." --
are all gated behind --enable-log-requests, and there is no completion line at
all, gated or not (grep for a logger.info on the finish path in v1/ returns
nothing). A reporter running 0.28.0 with the flag on read 1473 Added / 0
finished / 25 Aborted over 21.5 h of serving (syv-ai/qwen38-27b-rtx3090#94),
which is why a completed request, a client-aborted one and a request that
leaves the running set for some other reason are indistinguishable in a log
after the fact, and why the 2026-09-10 event in that issue is permanently
unclassifiable.

The line carries the request id, the finish reason, both token counts and the
wall time since arrival, at INFO and ungated. finish_reason is in scope at the
insert site: 0.28.0 captures it just above, before _handle_stopped_request may
reset the status to WAITING for a streaming request that continues, so the
value logged is the one the client sees. time and request.arrival_time /
request.num_prompt_tokens are already imported / present in 0.28.0.

Measured on the reference 3090 (0.28.0, CTX=fast, SPEC=dflash2, DFLASH_TOKENS=15,
one boot): 20 sequential 400-token streaming completions plus one 44,820-token
prefill produced exactly 21 lines, each matching what the client counted --
generated_tokens=400 against the client's completion_tokens=400 on all twenty,
and elapsed_s within 0.02 s of the client's wall time. A 21st request whose
client was SIGKILLed mid-stream produced the two abort lines and NO finish
line, which is the discriminator #94 was missing.

--- exported from cpuchip/vllm 613d76839 (engine-completion-log); regenerate with scripts/export-patch.sh, do not edit ---

diff --git a/v1/core/sched/scheduler.py b/v1/core/sched/scheduler.py
index 83ed59799..6bd6bc5e2 100644
--- a/v1/core/sched/scheduler.py
+++ b/v1/core/sched/scheduler.py
@@ -2059,6 +2059,20 @@
                 finished = self._handle_stopped_request(request)
                 if finished:
                     kv_transfer_params, ec_transfer_params = self._free_request(request)
+                    # 0.28.0 logged zero request-completion lines (1473 "Added"
+                    # lines vs 0 finish lines in 21.5 h of serving on a single
+                    # 3090), which made a completed request, a silently dropped
+                    # one, and a wedged one indistinguishable in the log. Emit
+                    # one line per request that leaves the scheduler finished.
+                    logger.info(
+                        "Request finished: req %s finish_reason=%s "
+                        "prompt_tokens=%d generated_tokens=%d elapsed_s=%.2f",
+                        request.request_id,
+                        getattr(finish_reason, "type", finish_reason),
+                        request.num_prompt_tokens,
+                        len(request.output_token_ids),
+                        max(0.0, time.time() - request.arrival_time),
+                    )
 
                 if status_before_stop == RequestStatus.RUNNING:
                     stopped_running_reqs.add(request)
